  "L3_learner_selection_meaning": "both learners are IN L3's class by design, so L3 selecting one is expected rather than an error. Where it happens the rung stops being an independent benchmark for that cell: it is the learner, re-measured on the evaluation stream, and cannot evidence that the learner beats a benchmark.",
  "selection_noise_caveat": "L3 names the member with the smallest SELECTION-stream mean. That is a noisy procedure: where the runner-up sits within about one standard error, a different selection draw would often name a different member. The frozen choice is still evaluated honestly on the held-out stream -- this caveat bounds what the choice means, not whether it is valid.",
